{"id":"h225","run":2,"role":"calibration","category":"science-physics","question":"The magnitude of the electrostatic force between two identical ions that are separated by a distance of $5.0 \\times 10^{-10} \\mathrm{~m}$ is $3.7 \\times 10^{-9}$ N.  What is the charge of each ion?\nIs the correct answer \"$3.2$ $10^{-19} \\mathrm{C}$\"?","truth":"yes","model_answer":"yes","correct":true,"source":"TIGER-Lab/MMLU-Pro, test split","claims":[{"text":"The charge of each ion is 3.2e-19 C.","confidence":0.95,"lean":1,"theta":1.4923,"phi":0.0},{"text":"Coulomb's law F = kq^2/r^2 gives q = r*sqrt(F/k).","confidence":0.97,"lean":1,"theta":1.5237,"phi":0.0},{"text":"Substituting the given values yields q ≈ 3.2e-19 C.","confidence":0.95,"lean":1,"theta":1.4923,"phi":0.0},{"text":"The result is about 2e, a whole-number multiple of the elementary charge, as expected for ions.","confidence":0.9,"lean":1,"theta":1.4137,"phi":0.0},{"text":"The sign of the charge cannot be determined from the magnitude alone.","confidence":0.9,"lean":0.0,"theta":1.4137,"phi":0.0},{"text":"The sign ambiguity does not count against the answer because the question asks only for magnitude.","confidence":0.9,"lean":1,"theta":1.4137,"phi":0.0},{"text":"The result depends on rounding of the given values.","confidence":0.6,"lean":-1,"theta":0.9425,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"The match to 2e is close enough that rounding does not change the conclusion.","confidence":0.88,"lean":1,"theta":1.3823,"phi":0.0},{"text":"The direct calculation and the physical check agree, which decides the answer as yes.","confidence":0.92,"lean":1,"theta":1.4451,"phi":0.0}],"relations":[{"i":0,"j":1,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":2,"J":0.9,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":3,"J":0.7,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":5,"J":0.3,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":7,"J":0.5,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":8,"J":0.7,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":2,"J":0.7,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":8,"J":0.3,"relation":"supports"},